# GPSS Java migration

This branch rewrites the backend in Java 21 + Spring Boot. The live mobile/web contract is frozen.

## Before writing Java

1. Read `docs/JAVA_REWRITE.md` for the module you are touching.
2. Read the matching Python files under `app/modules/<feature>/` and `tests/test_<feature>_flow.py`.
3. Preserve paths, status codes, error `code` strings, cookie name/path/flags, and JSON property names (including mixed camelCase / snake_case).

## Do

- Feature packages: `com.gpss.backend.{auth,attendance,clientlog,leave,upload}`
- Controllers thin, services own rules, repositories JPA only
- Flyway for schema; baseline existing Postgres; no `ddl-auto`
- Argon2 that verifies existing `users.password_hash` values
- Location ping business rejects as HTTP 200 `{ accepted: false, reason }`

## Do not

- Change the API to "idiomatic Spring" (e.g. 401 for GPS rejects, BCrypt-only, refresh token in JSON)
- Global Jackson `SNAKE_CASE`
- Raw SQL in services
- Add live-tracking WebSockets before HTTP parity
- Delete or "clean up" Python `app/` until Java MockMvc matches `tests/`
